From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 17:05:27 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] clk: sunxi-ng: a733-cpu: Park the DSU on the 600 MHz
 peripheral clock

While the DSU's PLL relocks, the DSU runs from the 26 MHz oscillator. The
DSU clocks the L3 cache and the snoop filter that all eight cores go
through, so the whole memory side slows down for every change of the DSU
rate.

Park the DSU on pll-periph0-600m instead, the DSU mux's encoding 101,
which the manual names as one of the DSU's backup sources (5.1.4.1),
when it runs at 600 MHz. That is below the DSU rate the boot loader sets
at the lowest voltage of the supply, so the park never runs the DSU
faster than the supply allows. probe() holds the clock enabled, so it
cannot be gated under a parked DSU, and defers until the main CCU
provides it. probe() makes the choice once and says which source it
took.

Not covered: changing the DSU rate; nothing does that yet.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: booted on two boards; probe reports the park
of the DSU on pll-periph0-600m, and with the DSU devfreq driver of the
following series stepping the DSU over all its points, up and down, the
mux reads back on the PLL after every step of the pair tests.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-sun60i-a733-cpu.c | 29 +++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 28 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-sun60i-a733-cpu.c b/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-sun60i-a733-cpu.c
index 9a1e88cfdff3..1cbf2e08ebde 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-sun60i-a733-cpu.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-sun60i-a733-cpu.c
@@ -102,6 +102,8 @@
 /* Mux indices are the encodings */
 #define CPU_MUX_SLOW		0
 #define CPU_CORE_MUX_BACK	5
+#define CPU_DSU_MUX_PERI0_600M	5
+#define CPU_DSU_PARK_RATE	600000000UL
 
 /*
  * Operating points that the core clusters and the DSU run at the lowest
@@ -784,11 +786,30 @@ static void sun60i_a733_cpu_park_on_back(struct device *dev)
 	dev_info(dev, "core clusters park on the backup PLL at %lu Hz\n", rate);
 }
 
+/*
+ * Park the DSU on pll-periph0-600m instead of cpu-slow when it runs at
+ * 600 MHz. probe() holds it enabled, so it cannot be gated under a parked
+ * DSU.
+ */
+static void sun60i_a733_cpu_park_dsu(struct device *dev, struct clk *peri0)
+{
+	unsigned long rate = clk_get_rate(peri0);
+
+	if (rate != CPU_DSU_PARK_RATE) {
+		dev_info(dev, "pll-periph0-600m at %lu Hz, the DSU parks on cpu-slow\n",
+			 rate);
+		return;
+	}
+
+	cpu_dsu_mux_nb.bypass_index = CPU_DSU_MUX_PERI0_600M;
+	dev_info(dev, "the DSU parks on pll-periph0-600m\n");
+}
+
 static int sun60i_a733_cpu_ccu_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 {
 	struct device *dev = &pdev->dev;
 	void __iomem *reg;
-	struct clk *hosc;
+	struct clk *hosc, *peri0;
 	unsigned int i;
 	int ret;
 
@@ -804,11 +825,17 @@ static int sun60i_a733_cpu_ccu_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
+	peri0 = devm_clk_get_enabled(dev, "pll-periph0-600m");
+	if (IS_ERR(peri0))
+		return dev_err_probe(dev, PTR_ERR(peri0),
+				     "cannot enable pll-periph0-600m\n");
+
 	ret = sun60i_a733_cpu_register_clks(dev, reg);
 	if (ret)
 		return dev_err_probe(dev, ret, "cannot register the clocks\n");
 
 	sun60i_a733_cpu_park_on_back(dev);
+	sun60i_a733_cpu_park_dsu(dev, peri0);
 
 	for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(sun60i_a733_cpu_clusters); i++) {
 		ret = sun60i_a733_cpu_register_nb(dev,
